# 0090-nas-covers-full-reads.patch -- the owner's field log of 2026-11-21 23:51: every .nsp and .nsz cover on the NAS "read failed: ResultFsOutOfRange (2002-3005)". Applies after
# 0089. UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, its pure part ran in the host harness, and the failure and its fix were reproduced with the app's LibHac (below).
#
# CAUSE (measured): GameIconsStream.Read puts the remote stream in LibHac's StreamStorage, whose read is ONE Stream.Read that takes a short count as the whole answer; SSH.NET's
#   SftpFileStream.Read gives what one SFTP reply holds. With LibHac 0.19.0 and a stream that gives at most 7 bytes per Read, PartitionFileSystem.Initialize fails with exactly
#   ResultFsOutOfRange (2002-3005) (probe90); a full-read stream (a file in Files) reads the same package. The .nup covers were not hit: NupRemote.Read already loops.
# FIX: RemoteReadStream (GameAppField.cs): between a remote stream and anything that expects full reads, every Read fills what was asked (up to the end of the file) from aligned 256 KB
#   blocks fetched with as many remote reads as needed and kept in a 16-block LRU (LibHac's many small header reads cost few round trips); Length is the size the listing's attributes
#   give; a remote file shorter than listed ends there. Every NAS read stream goes through it: the covers' shared session (Nas.WithSession) and Nas.WithReadStream. Each NAS cover logs
#   its cost: "cover: <game> (On the NAS): read in 3 requests, 768 KB".
# The .nup "carries no icon" (Ocarina): real for its BASE package (DEVICE-FINDINGS 2026-11-20: its meta has the NPDM and three small records, no NACP, no icon). In the same series,
#   crates/ibuilder-nup icon_of now falls back, when the base carries none, to the icon the BUILD writes (the newest update's control records, extract::control_meta), with a test; whether
#   the owner's container has an update package with an icon is not known here.
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-22, M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: every patch applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree. Compile (-t:Compile):
#   0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as before 0080. Host harness (harness90: … P89;P90): 303 of 303 checks (9 new: 400 random reads over 7-byte reads full and identical,
#   seek/length/end, one request for 2,000 small reads, the LRU, a short remote file, the log line, the wiring); 7 of 7 mutations killed. probe90 (LibHac 0.19.0, a synthetic PFS0 with an
#   icon file): full stream -> the bytes; 7-byte reads into StreamStorage -> ResultFsOutOfRange (2002-3005); the same through RemoteReadStream -> the SAME bytes; 32 KB replies -> 8 requests.
# NOT VERIFIED: a real NAS cover read (SSH.NET's reply size, the real request counts), a real NCA's control data through it.
# NEW LOG LINES: "cover: … (On the NAS): read in N requests, M KB" (" request", " requests, ", " KB").
